    "_comment": "The agent.sh commands a run-location: vm step may call through the forwarder (src/control/forwarder.js), each with the argument positions (0-based, after the command) that hold the project, ticket, variation and agent names: every one must match the calling VM's binding (an agent: one assigned to that ticket variation); and those that hold stdin, which must be \"-\": the content on stdin (ASS-182: /mnt/ticket is read-only, and no path reaches the Mac). A rule's \"max-args\" caps how many arguments the command may be given (ASS-298: work:write's optional trailing file path is the Mac's alone — a VM gives the content on stdin, never a path). A rule with \"fast-track\": true runs only for a VM whose ticket is fast-tracked (ASS-151: a golden-image rebuild ticket's host work; its project argument any project's). A command not listed is refused. validate.js fails a vm step whose script or prompt calls one missing here.",
